# ── RouteIQ Environment Variables ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your values.
# The ".env" file is gitignored and must NEVER be committed to source control.
#
# ── DATABASE (Neon.tech PostgreSQL) ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Sign up at https://neon.tech (free tier is sufficient)
# 2. Create a project named "routeiq"
# 3. From your Neon dashboard → Connection Details, copy the
#    "Connection string" (it looks like the line below).
# 4. Paste it here:
#
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://routeiq_owner:<password>@ep-<endpoint>.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/routeiq?sslmode=require
#
# ── Notes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# • If DATABASE_URL is NOT set, the app falls back to a local SQLite file at
#   data/routeiq.db — useful for offline development / testing.
# • On deployment platforms (Render, Railway, Fly.io, etc.) set DATABASE_URL
#   as a secret environment variable instead of using a .env file.
